{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november","id":1420548,"title":"[Aberrant] Aberrant in November","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-27T14:24:42-07:00","id":1420548,"title":"[Aberrant] Aberrant in November","content":"So the monthly kickstarter update came out for Aberrant and in it there was a hint and a nudge that Aberrant might come out in November. He didn't say whether it was early or mid or late, though he hinted it might be early-mid, hehe. <br /> <br /> I obviously don't have any other information to share but I figured I would mention this. <br /> <br /> While its not an announcement of an Adventure! kickstarter it is pretty awesome to hear that Aberrant is gonna be in our hands (figuratively speaking as its the pdf and not the pod) soon. <br /> <br /> I am so going to devour the powers chapter because I want to see what was added, changed, updated, expanded upon etc. So very much looking forward to creating a mostly Mega-Attribute (forgot the current term so pardon me using older terms) enhancement focused nova. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T14:27:34-07:00","id":1420549,"title":"","content":"I refuse to speculate on when the PDF will arrive, but I will be excited when it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T17:41:00-07:00","id":1420596,"title":"","content":"I hope I get it as a birthday gift (November 9, if any one want to aim the delivery), but I am not sure if it\u2019s going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T03:49:32-07:00","id":1420643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1420596#post1420596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope I get it as a birthday gift (November 9, if any one want to aim the delivery), but I am not sure if it\u2019s going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scorpio lol<br /> <br /> Awesome! I got it on BackerKit so I should get it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:04:43-07:00","id":1420998,"title":"","content":"They just sent out a Kickstarter email saying that over the next day or so the link to the drivethru page will be given in order to get the backer pdf. This is brilliant, spectacular news! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT - Just got the email link, just downloaded it now, just going through it as we speak! This is the best Halloween treat one could have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT 2 - Skipped to the character creation chapter and I already love what you guys did for Transcendence. Its a small change, removing monster and making it Other, probably just some sentences, but it feels soooo much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-30-2020, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:34:35-07:00","id":1421004,"title":"","content":"Woo! I know what I'm reading tonight!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:58:01-07:00","id":1421011,"title":"","content":"So with the Prodigy merit a nova gains access to a particular skill's skill tricks. Which is cool. But they still have to spend Momentum, in addition to quantum, which is less cool. So I was wondering on maybe removing the momentum cost and just allowing such a nova to use quantum to activate said trick.<br /> <br /> So they kept the whole psion-specific dominance on mental powers. I was hoping they would modify or honestly remove that side bar since the idea of niche protection seems out of place, especially since psiads themselves can do quantum stuff through QK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-30-2020, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:36:48-07:00","id":1421020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421011#post1421011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they kept the whole psion-specific dominance on mental powers. I was hoping they would modify or honestly remove that side bar since the idea of niche protection seems out of place, especially since psiads themselves can do quantum stuff through QK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but human Psions being capable of Quantum manipulation is a big setting shaking deal. I'm comfortable with Nova &quot;clairvoyance&quot; coming from Mega-Mental observation and deducation, and Nova &quot;mind control&quot; coming from Mega-Social influence. It's not like they're lacking in those areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:38:15-07:00","id":1421021,"title":"","content":"To repeat what I said on Discord: a lot of the discussion around the Kickstarter turned pretty toxic. We don't want to see more of that. Critique is fine, but please make sure you temper your comments and remember there are humans on the other end. Thank you.<br /> <br /> (And please make sure to use the errata form if you have corrections.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:38:23-07:00","id":1421022,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a chance to read yet: do Novas need a special Merit for Skill Tricks? I thought Skill Tricks were universal - even actual Baseline PCs have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:51:22-07:00","id":1421027,"title":"","content":"On the psychic thing, honestly, I'm just gong to say I basically fundamentally disagree with the restriction imposed and will be ignoring it in my games. <br /> <br /> Considering all that I love so far upon reading the book I don't want to dwell to much on the one tiny sidebar. <br /> <br /> Heck, I skipped to the end where it talks about Divis Mal and I loved what they did to him as well. Its not major changes but the description is a bit nice. <br /> <br /> So yeah, its a very impressive work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421022#post1421022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had a chance to read yet: do Novas need a special Merit for Skill Tricks? I thought Skill Tricks were universal - even actual Baseline PCs have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal rules still apply when it comes to Novas and skill tricks. This is a Mega-Edge that modifies how it works by allowing them to pick from any skill trick while adding a quantum point. <br /> <br /> I just thought if you spend XP on a Mega-Edge then the whole need to spend Momentum should be removed. <br /> <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> As a random thing one of the first Mega-Edges I want to bring back will be Sanitized Metabolism. hehe. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:09:37-07:00","id":1421030,"title":"","content":"The Quantum point is to give you the access, but it still requires the Momentum to power it, which seems fair to me. The ability to access whichever skill trick you want under a skill seems worth a Quantum point to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:18:18-07:00","id":1421033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421030#post1421030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Quantum point is to give you the access, but it still requires the Momentum to power it, which seems fair to me. The ability to access whichever skill trick you want under a skill seems worth a Quantum point to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Okay. I see. I will have to think more on this. <br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> So they didn't modify the Body Manipulation Mega-Edge. Its still got a dot rating and is still 12 XP for those modifications. It still seems a little pricy for what one gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-30-2020, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T13:39:04-07:00","id":1421047,"title":"","content":"There are a few typos, but the scale table on page 164 is *chef's kiss*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T16:58:57-07:00","id":1421067,"title":"","content":"So ya, super excited to see the backer PDF come in my email this morning. Look through and half read while waking up and love the layout and it looks pretty tight. I'm defiantly on team &quot;Wave the mental powers restrict&quot; which thanks to the Continuum nature of the game makes it easy. The expanded scale system is amazing!!! That was well worth a wait in my opinion. I do have a few questions. Which I'll throw up on another thread. All in all however so happy to see this game get some pretty awesome new life breathed into it! Can't wait for Adventure!!! Will be great to have all three base games on the shelf with their 1e counterparts. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T19:05:29-07:00","id":1421082,"title":"","content":"In the final draft of the PDF will the names of the Elemental Themes on page 210 be in bold. The names of each of the elemental types gets lost in the text really easy as it stands now. Not sure if that would count as a errata or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T19:17:56-07:00","id":1421084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421082#post1421082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the final draft of the PDF will the names of the Elemental Themes on page 210 be in bold. The names of each of the elemental types gets lost in the text really easy as it stands now. Not sure if that would count as a errata or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely put that in errata","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:20:26-07:00","id":1421104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421027#post1421027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal rules still apply when it comes to Novas and skill tricks. This is a Mega-Edge that modifies how it works by allowing them to pick from any skill trick while adding a quantum point.<br /> <br /> I just thought if you spend XP on a Mega-Edge then the whole need to spend Momentum should be removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Skill Tricks cost 3 xp. Mega-Edges cost 12 xp. Every Skill from the core book lists three to four associated Skill Tricks, so you can just spend 9 to 12 xp and save your Quantum points (you may also save the point of Flux you take for learning the Mega-Edge after character creation). The Mega-Edge would only be considered a good use of xp if you have access to a bunch of additional pre-made Skill Tricks, or your group is fine with you making very frequent use of the Skill Trick design rules.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed with the PDF - and I'm not sure if this is a design feature or an oversight that needs an errata submission - is the Warp power's Impose tag. It looks like you need a number of successes equal to their Defense + 3 to suck someone through a wormhole. Since your maximum normal dice pool is 16 (Quantum 9 + Warp 7), a completely mundane human with a decent Defense has a good chance of ignoring Divis Mal's attempt to telefrag him. While I understand they don't want players derailing adventures with constant warp gate telefrags, these rules seem to make it virtually impossible for anyone less powerful than an elder Aberrant to use the option, and it doesn't stop your grapple monster buddy from just grabbing the guy and throwing him through anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T22:49:13-07:00","id":1421118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421104#post1421104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill Tricks cost 3 xp. Mega-Edges cost 12 xp. Every Skill from the core book lists three to four associated Skill Tricks, so you can just spend 9 to 12 xp and save your Quantum points (you may also save the point of Flux you take for learning the Mega-Edge after character creation). The Mega-Edge would only be considered a good use of xp if you have access to a bunch of additional pre-made Skill Tricks, or your group is fine with you making very frequent use of the Skill Trick design rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes the book assumes you are not treating those lists as exhaustive as they are not meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T22:53:33-07:00","id":1421120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421104#post1421104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill Tricks cost 3 xp. Mega-Edges cost 12 xp. Every Skill from the core book lists three to four associated Skill Tricks, so you can just spend 9 to 12 xp and save your Quantum points (you may also save the point of Flux you take for learning the Mega-Edge after character creation). The Mega-Edge would only be considered a good use of xp if you have access to a bunch of additional pre-made Skill Tricks, or your group is fine with you making very frequent use of the Skill Trick design rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It becomes XP efficient if you only have 1 dot in the skill you use Prodigy for. Normally, you'd have to spend 10xp to get up to 3 dots, and then spend the 9-12xp for all of the skill tricks.<br /> <br /> ETA: You need 5 dots in a skill to have 3 skill tricks. So, you can't normally have access to 4 at a time, and you'll need to factor in the cost of 4 more skill dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 10-31-2020, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T08:29:24-07:00","id":1421162,"title":"","content":"So at this point the biggest thing I don't understand from a choice perspective is Body Modification. 12 XP for each dot of things in that Mega-Edge seems unduly expensive for what one gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T08:57:02-07:00","id":1421166,"title":"","content":"I think the fact they cost no Quantum Points to use and are always on/available is supposed to account for the 12 xp. Does it? I don't know.<br /> <br /> ETA: They might also be immune to Quantum Disruption. I've put a question into the errata as to whether Quantum Disruption only applies to things under the Quantum Powers heading or if it also applies to Mega-Attributes and/or -Edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 10-31-2020, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T14:48:36-07:00","id":1421215,"title":"","content":"So, confusion. While the Scale chart is pretty handy what I am not entirely sure on is how the Mega-Attributes interact with it. Like when and how does Mega-Cunning dots translate into Scale. I mean is Initiative the only thing it gains a scale on? But that doesn't seem right. So yeah, confusion on when Scale applies.<br /> <br /> I have been assuming that Mega-Attributes apply both Scale and Enhancements whenever one does something using the base Attribute. So when one rolls Cunning then they get a Scale bonus for having Mega-Cunning, the same for the eight other Attributes and their Mega-Attributes.<br /> <br /> Is that wrong? Right? Blue? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> So I just realized that a stealth star Nova with Hypnotic Presence might basically only roll 2 dice for the hypnotic action if they are Quantum 1 and Mega-Manipulation 1. That is not a very high chance of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-31-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:16:13-07:00","id":1421219,"title":"","content":"Mega-Cunning gives you speed scale equal to M-C dots for initiative and Keen Senses with enhancements equal to M-C dots. That's it, RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:23:29-07:00","id":1421222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421219#post1421219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mega-Cunning gives you speed scale equal to M-C dots for initiative and Keen Senses with enhancements equal to M-C dots. That's it, RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a waste. It also doesn't seem to truly cover what the Mega-Attribute does in flavor. <br /> <br /> So what am I missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:25:34-07:00","id":1421223,"title":"","content":"Based on Mega-Stamina not giving defense scale, and on Mega-Dex not giving any bonus on Aim OR Speed let alone scale without a mega-edge, my current assumption is that Mega-Atts ONLY give some form of bonus on things they very specifically specify in the entry.<br /> <br /> So Mega-Cunning ONLY gives you Scale on Initiative, and dots in Keen Senses edges. Rolling cunning to lie? No benefit.<br /> <br /> I honestly feel like Mega-Atts got nerfed to hard from the original game, but they're still neat and useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:29:39-07:00","id":1421224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421223#post1421223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on Mega-Stamina not giving defense scale, and on Mega-Dex not giving any bonus on Aim OR Speed let alone scale without a mega-edge, my current assumption is that Mega-Atts ONLY give some form of bonus on things they very specifically specify in the entry.<br /> <br /> So Mega-Cunning ONLY gives you Scale on Initiative, and dots in Keen Senses edges. Rolling cunning to lie? No benefit.<br /> <br /> I honestly feel like Mega-Atts got nerfed to hard from the original game, but they're still neat and useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>So its not that I missed things its that they changed the assumption so much that what I thought was there, what I figured would be there, is actually gone and I didn't notice since I was mostly focused on what I expected it to be. <br /> <br /> Yeah, that bothers me. I mean why shouldn't Mega-Cunning help with lying. Why does it only help with initiative. <br /> <br /> I really thought that the Mega-Attributes provided scale naturally to actions undertaking their base Attribute. I see that it does for some, like Mega-Intellect, but not all of them. <br /> <br /> I don't get that. <br /> <br /> So again, what am I missing. There has to be some sort of reason. <br /> <br /> Otherwise yeah, its a nerf, and it is not so great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:39:25-07:00","id":1421226,"title":"","content":"I think they just saw over the years that Mega-Atts in 1st ed were really really good, and they decided that if they gave scale on everything they'd be too good. Which I personally don't agree with but it is what it is. As far as I can tell Mega-Atts literally only do things they explicitly say they do. <br /> <br /> Like I'm not certain, but based on the wording I think Mega-Might provides scale for say, Rolling JUST might to rip a bank vault door off, but DOES NOT provide scale when you roll Might + Close Combat to punch someone. So if you've got 2 might, 2 mega-might, and 1 close combat, you can pick up a car like I pick up my cat, and you can tear through a wall more easily than I can open a banana, but you still only get 3 dice if you punch something.<br /> <br /> This may be a gross misunderstanding on my part, but that's how it reads to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:55:54-07:00","id":1421227,"title":"","content":"Further thoughts.<br /> I don't like that Accuracy (p 186) doesn't grant scale.<br /> I don't like that there appears to be NO way to add Mega-Might to your Close Combat. Not like Shockwave or Thunderclap, but actually like &quot;You gain Dots Scale to your Might based attacks&quot;. I'd be perfectly happy with a setup where it was Prereq: Dots x 2 Mega-Might. But going from &quot;Mega-Strength gives you 5 auto-successes per dot on Str based combat and damage rolls&quot; to &quot;Being Punched by a Nova with 5 Mega-Might and being punched by a Baseline with NO POWERS AT ALL with 5 Might are EXACTLY THE SAME&quot; is a bit weird. (Ok, the nova's gonna do more damage because his target number is lower, but the MEGA-might is doing nothing for him)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T16:02:33-07:00","id":1421228,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry for flooding, but I feel like I need to take a second to say, I am actually really happy with almost everything in the new version of Aberrant. None of these complaints will stop me from playing or enjoying the game. I feel like we sometimes come off overly negative, and I may have here, because it's easier to call out specific things we AREN'T happy with than to call out what we like.<br /> <br /> There are things I wish had been done differently, but I really like the game, I'm really happy it's gotten an update and new content coming, and I'm really happy that Trinity continuum is a living supported game line again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T16:05:45-07:00","id":1421229,"title":"","content":"I was thinking on a starting character that is a stealth nova with Mega-Attributes of 1 in eight or nine Attributes and three or four Mega-Edges. Due to the nature of the rules of where Mega-Attributes apply there are entire areas where they are not doing things mechanically more potent then baselines. While in my head, with Mega-Attributes give scale equal to rating, they are at Scale 2 in everything they do. Which is what I figured would make logical sense. <br /> <br /> The nerf that seems to now exist makes me hope I am just missing something. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T17:05:22-07:00","id":1421233,"title":"","content":"A comment on Scale on Attack and Defense:<br /> <br /> No power cause scale on attacks or defense, except Speed and only if the target is moving, not during a close combat fight. The scales apply only to damage, and durability don\u2019t make the targets more capable or dodging.<br /> <br /> Mega Might can cause much more damage, but the nova can\u2019t be particularly more capable in hitting just for being strong. The scale enhancements applies only to causing damage, including critical, what is particularly useful as you can also buy multiple injuries. So, don\u2019t hit often, but a hit can be lethal really fast...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T17:09:30-07:00","id":1421235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421227#post1421227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further thoughts.<br /> I don't like that Accuracy (p 186) doesn't grant scale.<br /> I don't like that there appears to be NO way to add Mega-Might to your Close Combat. Not like Shockwave or Thunderclap, but actually like &amp;quot;You gain Dots Scale to your Might based attacks&amp;quot;. I'd be perfectly happy with a setup where it was Prereq: Dots x 2 Mega-Might. But going from &amp;quot;Mega-Strength gives you 5 auto-successes per dot on Str based combat and damage rolls&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Being Punched by a Nova with 5 Mega-Might and being punched by a Baseline with NO POWERS AT ALL with 5 Might are EXACTLY THE SAME&amp;quot; is a bit weird. (Ok, the nova's gonna do more damage because his target number is lower, but the MEGA-might is doing nothing for him)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think where they mention increases power scale for damaging things, covers people as well. So as long as you pay of the difficulty to cover a targets defense then you would add scale and ability to punch through a normal baseline at mega-might 2 or 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T23:44:02-07:00","id":1421262,"title":"","content":"So quick question--for those of us who weren't able to back it, does anyone have any hints on when the drive thru copies will drop for purchase?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T00:01:14-07:00","id":1421264,"title":"","content":"So as Steve did most of the system on powers, and maybe most of the rest of the book(not sure) there is a lot of compare and contrast to 1e as well as M&amp;M 3e. So with the power tags adding in AOE abilities does it feel like a selective tag is missing. So for instance using a gravity field to increase gravity on an area and selectively not hitting team mates with it, or using Quantum Anima as an area but only moving select things vs everything. Or maybe even a teleport with area and selective so you can easily move your friends and you in and out of locations without bringing everything, like say half a building with you causing massive damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T00:03:14-07:00","id":1421265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421262#post1421262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quick question--for those of us who weren't able to back it, does anyone have any hints on when the drive thru copies will drop for purchase?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m bad with time but I think it\u2019s several weeks to a month or two for backer PDF errata to come in, then a few weeks to compile implement said errata. Then a one more good pass over by the dev team. So I\u2019d say 1 - 3 months at a shortest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T01:45:03-08:00","id":1421272,"title":"","content":"You can buy it on Aberrant Backerskit.<br /> I think the address is<br /> <a href=\"https://trinity-continuum-aberrant.backerkit.com/backer/review\" target=\"_blank\">https://trinity-continuum-aberrant.backerkit.com</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T04:43:37-08:00","id":1421280,"title":"","content":"re: mega-attributes and losing functions - most of those functions are purchasable as Mega-Edges that require the Mega-attribute, now. Given the amazing value Mega-attributes could be otherwise, I think it's a defensible choice to make.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T17:54:05-08:00","id":1421367,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know. I mean I doubt any of my problems or objections or concerns will be answered, commented on or whatnot and so I don't really think there is any point to worry about what is in the book as what it is it is. <br /> <br /> The thing that makes this all the more funny in a surprisingly sad way for me is that Aberrant was the 1e game I loved the most (with Adventure! bit farther down as second) while in the Continuum I like Aeon the most (and from the way they wrote Talents I can see my liking of Adventure! staying second) and Aberrant a lot less. This isn't even the settings chapter, which I sort of ignore in both Aberrant and Aeon, in both 1e and 2e but the powers chapter - Aeon boosted psions up to a spectacularly fun level while it feels like Aberrant nerfed novas quite a bit. <br /> <br /> I created a character using the 150 points, giving him 9 Mega-Attributes (all at 1) and three Mega-Edges. Going by the rules as is he is basically not that far from regular baseline in what I as a player could do in many ways. And I don't like that. Where is the whole &quot;power of a god' or 'you can be a superhero' tag element that was at the core of the game. <br /> <br /> This all said, I gotta give them sooooooooooooo much credit. I am so glad that Onyx bought Trinity and I am extremely glad that Ian pushed them to bring it back. I just wish they didn't do it in such a way that it feels to me that novas get the short end of the stick like it seems they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T18:30:56-08:00","id":1421371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421367#post1421367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I created a character using the 150 points, giving him 9 Mega-Attributes (all at 1) and three Mega-Edges. Going by the rules as is he is basically not that far from regular baseline in what I as a player could do in many ways. And I don't like that. Where is the whole &quot;power of a god' or 'you can be a superhero' tag element that was at the core of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have intentionally designed a jack of all trades, master of none, so it's not surprising that he feels less powerful than a Nova who invests in higher Quantum and building up a specific Mega-Attribute or two, or investing in their power set.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T18:47:56-08:00","id":1421373,"title":"","content":"As well, the whole thing feels a bit more continuous when a single dot in a Mega-Attribute <i>isn't</i> enough to let you trounce baselines every time. It gives me some gray area to work with for my \u201cstealth Novas\u201d who I <i>don't</i> want coming across as overtly superhuman: that's why they're <u>stealth</u> Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T18:54:19-08:00","id":1421374,"title":"","content":"A fun project to work on at some point is what a low rating in an attribute + a Mega dot actually looks like compared to a higher rating in an Attribute without Megas.<br /> <br /> Thaddeus Venture is a good touchstone that's been suggested before as someone with low-average Intellect, but a single dot of Mega-Intellect.<br /> <br /> Lower Might but with a dot of Mega-Might could play out lack of finer control of the application of your super-strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T18:57:19-08:00","id":1421376,"title":"","content":"Interesting that I have a feeling that is almost the opposite.<br /> <br /> Not on the average power of a Nova, I have the feeling that a initial nova is slightly less powerful on TC than was in 1e, but only if you want to be a generalist nova. A focused Nova can be absolutely more powerful than a 1e, using Power Suites you can do a lot of things with a little XP. Also Power Stunts and Maxing out, but they are another thing...<br /> <br /> My feeling about powers and Mega-things is, the numbers are low, but the focus is in the narrative. Scale 2 is something else, very powerful, Speed 2 can keep the sprinter speed during a marathon, Might 2 can lift a truck with some effort, Power 2 is equivalent to a .50 machine gun. Scale 3 is even more, going an entire level above it.<br /> <br /> Most X-men are around scale 2 or 3 in their main powers (well, some writers may put them on a higher scale), of course there are a few that can cross this line, but it\u2019s perfectly possible using maxing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T19:16:41-08:00","id":1421379,"title":"","content":"Personally, I tend to view the relationship between Attribute and Mega-Attribute with the Mega-Attribute being dominant and the regular Attribute representing a fine-tuning of your Mega-Attribute: someone with Mega-Might 1 and Might 1 is at the lower end of what Mega-Might 1 can do, while someone with Mega-Might 1 and Might 5 is at the upper end of Mega-Might 1. And instead of saying that you can't have a Mega-Attribute higher than its corresponding Attribute, I view it as you can't have an Attribute <i>lower than</i> its corresponding Mega-Attribute: someone with Might 1 is too weak to handle the rigors associated with Mega-Might 2. Mathematically, the two approaches are equivalent; but conceptually, this alternative interpretation makes more sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T19:20:57-08:00","id":1421380,"title":"","content":"(Will comment on other things once I take them in)<br /> <br /> I will say this though I think that all Mega-Attributes should effect Scale in some main way. The idea that Mega-Cunning only effects scale with Initiative seems to be lacking in putting the full power behind Cunning. Resolve and Dexterity don't effect scale at all. How is that logical?<br /> <br /> That said, I did just had a thought that there might be a benefit to having an eight category of Scale - Control. It would represent doing things precisely and with super-finesse. It could be quite useful with say certain elements of Dexterity and such things.<br /> <br /> The fact that a Mega-Attribute costs 12 XP and in some cases doesn't seem to do anything practical seems lacking to me. Everything I buy should do something, should give me something. Even if its simply another dice to roll in a pool. I mean I get why Mega-Attributes don't give extra dice, but then it should naturally give Enhancement for everything the base attribute does. This, I think, is where a big part of my problems come from.<br /> <br /> I mean if my character with Mega-Attributes of 1 in all nine attributes automatically gained a +1 scale and/or 2 Enhancements to whatever he did, then I would feel him being potent without being game breaking. He would feel superhuman. He would feel like he is on the path of having the power of a god, which is the tag of the game.<br /> <br /> But in a number of cases, Mega-Cunning for example, he doesn't. When he rolls say Cunning + Empathy his Mega-Cunning doesn't do anything.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, so I said this in another post but the way that Hypnotic Presence works seems designed with too high a chance of failure for me. Firstly, its dice pool is Quantum + Mega-Manipulation. Its not roll your normal dice pool and get Mega-Manipulation in Enhancement but straight up Quantum + Mega-Manipulation. That is not a really easy to use power. Especially considering the success costs for the difficulties of commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-01-2020, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T19:44:17-08:00","id":1421384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421380#post1421380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Will comment on other things once I take them in)<br /> <br /> I will say this though I think that all Mega-Attributes should effect Scale in some main way. The idea that Mega-Cunning only effects scale with Initiative seems to be lacking in putting the full power behind Cunning. Resolve and Dexterity don't effect scale at all. How is that logical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because parallelism on paper doesn't equal balance in gameplay. Initiative Scale is INSANELY powerful. Erasing Complications on movement is huge in large part because your movement rolls aren't generally going to have someone's opposing Scale, instead the challenge with play out through Complications that Mega-Dex erases.<br /> <br /> Resolve and Composure I do think could use a boost. One or both should grant Scale in resisting power-enhanced mental/social influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T07:44:28-08:00","id":1421444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421384#post1421384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because parallelism on paper doesn't equal balance in gameplay. Initiative Scale is INSANELY powerful. Erasing Complications on movement is huge in large part because your movement rolls aren't generally going to have someone's opposing Scale, instead the challenge with play out through Complications that Mega-Dex erases.<br /> <br /> Resolve and Composure I do think could use a boost. One or both should grant Scale in resisting power-enhanced mental/social influences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If absolute balance was an issue, I think they'd need it, but aren't influence checks something you can refuse automatically if you don't agree them (with little cost)?<br /> <br /> Edit: Nevermind just reread the Hypnotic Presence and compelling presence. Maybe they should add a power simillar to Sensory Shield to protect from those type of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","user":"Monkeydjie","date":". 11-02-2020, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:33:15-08:00","id":1421529,"title":"","content":"I am not asking that a Nova trounce a mortal in everything, all I am asking is that the player gets to do that which they are said to be able to do, and that is best formated by letting them use their powers. If something is supposed to represent superhuman attributes then they should apply in some form to everything the base attributes do. This apply can be 'free' with the gaining of the mega-attribute itself or via an associated Mega-Edge to boost the capability to a somewhat side direction. But to me if a dice pool has an attribute then one's mega-attribute should apply somehow.<br /> <br /> I say let there be narrative scale boost that translates to the whole 2 enhancements per difference from base - so a Mega-Attribute 1 person has 2 enhancements, 2 dots is 4 enhancements, etc while also sometimes being able to say he does things at a higher scale level then normal.<br /> <br /> Honestly, from reading some other threads in the internet I think many other people might think similarly - that having a Mega-Attribute they get automatic Scale equal to its rating for everything they do. The fact that this is not true is mind boggling to me.<br /> <br /> As is the fact that a nova's regular traits don't always get applied when they use certain Mega-Edges, like the hypnosis one I said above which is a roll of Quantum + Mega-Manipulation instead of say gaining the Mega-Edge adds the twist to one's normal abilities, and a boost to said manipulations by Mega-Manipulation. (In otherwords without the Mega-Edge the ability the power refers to cannot even be done in such a way, but with the Mega-Edge the nova now has the ability, boosted by his Mega-Manipulation rating.)<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also I am not knocking getting scale for Initiative when one has Mega-Cunning. I think that is cool and useful. But I also don't think it should be the main point for that mega-attribute because what happens in sessions that don't have combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Mega-Scent vs Mega-Cunning granted Keen Senses Edge<br /> <br /> As said, doesn't the Enhancement equal to Mega-Cunning that is granted in the Keen Senses (All) Edge apply to this, basically giving them Mega-Scent already? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-02-2020, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T18:26:13-08:00","id":1421896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421104#post1421104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I noticed with the PDF - and I'm not sure if this is a design feature or an oversight that needs an errata submission - is the Warp power's Impose tag. It looks like you need a number of successes equal to their Defense + 3 to suck someone through a wormhole. Since your maximum normal dice pool is 16 (Quantum 9 + Warp 7), a completely mundane human with a decent Defense has a good chance of ignoring Divis Mal's attempt to telefrag him. While I understand they don't want players derailing adventures with constant warp gate telefrags, these rules seem to make it virtually impossible for anyone less powerful than an elder Aberrant to use the option, and it doesn't stop your grapple monster buddy from just grabbing the guy and throwing him through anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely making an errata submission on Warp. Not only does it require a Defense + 3 roll to work, the Teleport power two pages earlier only requires rolling vs. Defense. Having just skimmed back through the core book, I've realized a Minor Threat Antagonist (the weakest non-minion antagonist) gets a Defense of 3. As written, you literally have to roll a minimum of 6 successes to affect anyone other than a stock minion, and even a minion seems to require 4-5 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T15:55:38-08:00","id":1422505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421529#post1421529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not asking that a Nova trounce a mortal in everything, all I am asking is that the player gets to do that which they are said to be able to do, and that is best formated by letting them use their powers. If something is supposed to represent superhuman attributes then they should apply in some form to everything the base attributes do. This apply can be 'free' with the gaining of the mega-attribute itself or via an associated Mega-Edge to boost the capability to a somewhat side direction. But to me if a dice pool has an attribute then one's mega-attribute should apply somehow.<br /> <br /> I say let there be narrative scale boost that translates to the whole 2 enhancements per difference from base - so a Mega-Attribute 1 person has 2 enhancements, 2 dots is 4 enhancements, etc while also sometimes being able to say he does things at a higher scale level then normal.<br /> <br /> Honestly, from reading some other threads in the internet I think many other people might think similarly - that having a Mega-Attribute they get automatic Scale equal to its rating for everything they do. The fact that this is not true is mind boggling to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back when the backer manuscript preview was released, I remember saying that we definitely needed more clarity about what the Mega-Attributes did and didn't apply to. The final book may be an improvement, but I feel things could be a lot more clear.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think what we need is a detailed example. &quot;Nova McExample has one dot in each of the nine Mega-Attributes, but no Mega-Edges. He gains bonuses A, B, and C but not X, Y, or Z, for which he would need...&quot;<br /> <br /> The ideal explanation might actually be a full checklist of the traits required for a nova to be &quot;superhuman&quot; in every meaningful respect -- which Mega-Edges are needed to fill in the blanks, as it were.<br /> <br /> (Aberrant 1e was a flawed game in many ways, but it was fairly easy to tell what your character actually needed to be super-everything: pretty much just Mega-Attributes plus Armor, and maybe Psychic Shield.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T17:01:43-08:00","id":1422516,"title":"","content":"Actually it said when you can use Mega Attributes, it don\u2019t say when you can\u2019t, but there is a very small list of RPGs that tell you what you can\u2019t do, so it\u2019s not that bad.<br /> <br /> I understand Mega Attribute are not as useful as they were in 1e, but I agree with the new edition and the limited uses of them. Having Mega Attributes made every roll irrelevant and every thing other than the mega attribute irrelevant to the roll.<br /> <br /> The new system give some weight to the Mega Attributes, but they don\u2019t make the rest irrelevant in the rolls.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Mega Attributes more important, you can roll the mega attribute with the attribute, so if you have a Athletics 3 + Strength 4 + Mega Strength 2 you roll 9 dice instead of 7. It would make it a bit better, but it would unbalance their use and many rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T21:13:11-08:00","id":1422538,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have a problem with the Mega-Attributes having only specific functions per se, but it gets complicated enough that IMO the exclusions should be more clearly called out.<br /> <br /> The flavor text for Mega-Stamina actually says it grants &quot;resistance to harm.&quot; You have to read the details pretty carefully to get the full picture, and I could easily see a new player genuinely reading the whole thing and not realizing what he's missing. It could really use a note like &quot;Mega-Stamina alone does not apply to <i>direct</i> damage from enemy attacks; if you're trying to build a super-tough nova, see Toughness, p. 197.&quot;<br /> <br /> And...hrm. I just noticed that the Accuracy Mega-Edge makes it sound as if Mega-Dexterity doesn't <i>normally</i> apply to combat rolls, but I don't see anything in the Mega-Dexterity entry that would prevent it from applying to ranged attacks just like any other Dexterity roll. Or am I missing some detail of the combat rules that would make Mega-Dexterity's difficulty reduction inapplicable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T02:37:03-08:00","id":1422572,"title":"","content":"MDex just reduces difficulties and complications (Defense is Difficulty), so it is useful but limited, while Accuracy grants enhancements, what is far more useful when dealing with easy targets. But MDex can be used in close combat while accuracy doesn\u2019t, as long the attack is made using dexterity, for example trying to scape from a grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T11:59:53-08:00","id":1422793,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I have to say, at first I was baffled to see &quot;a chess grandmaster&quot; as an example of mental Scale. Then I remembered that you can get Scale from a skill trick, which I assume is how you'd represent grandmastery in this system. (Although I am honestly not sure which of the sixteen skills would apply to a chess match.)<br /> <br /> So on that note, does a Scale boost from a skill trick stack with Mega-Attribute/Mega-Edge Scale? I had almost forgotten about skill tricks while reading all the crazy powers novas can get, but it does seem like a useful way to represent novas with some kind of specialized aptitude. (Like that guy with a superhuman sense of style who designs nova identities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T14:01:58-08:00","id":1422822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1422793#post1422793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I have to say, at first I was baffled to see &quot;a chess grandmaster&quot; as an example of mental Scale. Then I remembered that you can get Scale from a skill trick, which I assume is how you'd represent grandmastery in this system. (Although I am honestly not sure which of the sixteen skills would apply to a chess match.)<br /> <br /> So on that note, does a Scale boost from a skill trick stack with Mega-Attribute/Mega-Edge Scale? I had almost forgotten about skill tricks while reading all the crazy powers novas can get, but it does seem like a useful way to represent novas with some kind of specialized aptitude. (Like that guy with a superhuman sense of style who designs nova identities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Swift Edge grants +1 speed scale when running and only costs 1 dot, so I could easily accept cheap non-powered Edges that grant Scale in limited circumstances. Having a 1 dot Chessmaster Edge seems perfectly reasonable to me. I'd also make a game of chess default to Intellect+Enigmas (swap to Cunning for speed chess and Resolve for marathon chess matches).<br /> <br /> I also know that Psions and Psiads with the Biokinesis Enhance power can gain a speed scale boost that stacks with the Swift Edge, so I don't see why Novas wouldn't stack appropriate scale boosts as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:24:23-08:00","id":1422830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1422822#post1422822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Swift Edge grants +1 speed scale when running and only costs 1 dot, so I could easily accept cheap non-powered Edges that grant Scale in limited circumstances. Having a 1 dot Chessmaster Edge seems perfectly reasonable to me. I'd also make a game of chess default to Intellect+Enigmas (swap to Cunning for speed chess and Resolve for marathon chess matches).<br /> <br /> I also know that Psions and Psiads with the Biokinesis Enhance power can gain a speed scale boost that stacks with the Swift Edge, so I don't see why Novas wouldn't stack appropriate scale boosts as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point -- an Edge probably makes more sense than a skill trick, since a skill trick granting Scale apparently only works for one round, and a chess grandmaster could beat you in chess all day regardless of Momentum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:51:01-08:00","id":1422835,"title":"","content":"Rounds out of combat are a bit more flexible.<br /> <br /> You could make a chess match be a single test, a complex action or a sequence of moves, as long it\u2019s relevant to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:54:57-08:00","id":1422837,"title":"","content":"The chess master probably has a specialty that gives 3 enhancement on every chess related roll as well as an applicable skill trick or two to use on occasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T21:06:29-08:00","id":1422870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1422837#post1422837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chess master probably has a specialty that gives 3 enhancement on every chess related roll as well as an applicable skill trick or two to use on occasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Specialties is that they don't apply to the Skill in which you have the Specialty, so if chess is an Enigmas roll, you'd need something like Culture to specialize in chess as a popular game, Humanities to specialize in chess through a historical lens, or Empathy to get a read on your opponent. Maybe a world class chess player has three dots in multiple Skills (since it strains belief for them to have 5 in multiple Skills) and chess related Enhancements on all of them? Between that and a scale boosting Edge, I can see a chess master readily trouncing almost anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T06:01:36-08:00","id":1422900,"title":"","content":"You only need one of them to get the enhancement on all the others. Personally I think it is very weird the way specialties are done in Trinity and I personally don\u2019t run it that way. The idea isn\u2019t without merit, but its not for me and my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","user":"andrewm9","date":". 11-10-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T06:09:47-08:00","id":1422901,"title":"","content":"You could also take a specialty in strategy with Command.<br /> <br /> I really like the specialties in TC. They make a focused character a little better at other things and reward characters with bigger skill spreads with bonuses to lots of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T07:55:52-08:00","id":1422905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1422793#post1422793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I have to say, at first I was baffled to see &quot;a chess grandmaster&quot; as an example of mental Scale. Then I remembered that you can get Scale from a skill trick, which I assume is how you'd represent grandmastery in this system. (Although I am honestly not sure which of the sixteen skills would apply to a chess match.)<br /> <br /> So on that note, does a Scale boost from a skill trick stack with Mega-Attribute/Mega-Edge Scale? I had almost forgotten about skill tricks while reading all the crazy powers novas can get, but it does seem like a useful way to represent novas with some kind of specialized aptitude. (Like that guy with a superhuman sense of style who designs nova identities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make &quot;+1 Scale playing games of strategy&quot; an Enigmas Skill Trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that some people who are exceptional human beings in reality could be represented as Talents in the more cinematic universe of Trinity Continuum, and they also have various ways to reflect Scale between Gifts and the ability to spend Inspiration for +1 Scale as a universal power (also from the external perspective of playing chess against a Talent, you could just use Scale to reflect the Talent being so good because of dramatic editing making moves retroactively strategically correct).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T16:43:31-08:00","id":1422988,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about things and I find myself wishing that I didn't actually get to see the materials of the book before they are finished and done because if the book was out I would feel so much better going &quot;nope&quot; and then making house rules and changes and such on the numerous elements that I find disconcerting. But because the book isn't finished there is a hope that they will decide to change certain things, even if realistically said hope is not real because they won't. <br /> <br /> Its even more disappointing as out of all of the Trinity game lines I loved Aberrant the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T17:02:38-08:00","id":1422990,"title":"","content":"While I do have some concerns related to some rules (read Super Tech, and apply it all the way to Core), my general feeling about the book is very positive. It\u2019s a great improve over the original rules in general, you give much more flexibility on the way your character evolve and the way the game flows. The improvement is also above the original manuscript that have too many weak spot, and seams much more solid now.<br /> <br /> For sure I will House Rule the s***t out of it, just because there is always some space to work to adapt to this or that taste (in this case, my taste). I love game rules and how we can adapt different ideas to different systems, some times without even noticing the references.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would love to discuss how we can improve the game for your tastes. I am trying to create the Hit Points system you suggested, I really am, but I am on a more narrative tendency than used to be, and I keep moving back to a reduced number of hit points (health boxes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T17:24:51-08:00","id":1422994,"title":"","content":"While I do agree that there have been sections cleaned up and made better/easier to read I don't think if I would personally go very positive at this time .That said they did make some changes that are pretty good, like what they did to Transcendence and Flux. The things that I would like to see improved are the Mega-Attributes, the Body Modification Mega-Edge, and the lack of mental powers in the Quantum Power suite. I totally agree with some of the weirdness in the super tech stuff but I haven't fully delved into it. The same with the quantum powers, mostly because after reading the Mega-Attribute and Mega-Edge sections I found my interest in delving into the quantum power section to have waned a bit. The truth is that it has become less fun right now so I basically just closed my copy of the book and will probably open it again later on when its more enjoyable then it is now. <br /> <br /> On the hit point system while I won't say no, hehe, I actually get the way the health system works now, Its still not my favorite way of doing things but its okay and understandable now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T06:06:38-08:00","id":1423043,"title":"","content":"The Body Modification Mega Edge really is a problem on how it works, because they don\u2019t worth the XP in general.<br /> My approach to it is: they are \u201cbeneficial transformations\u201d, so you consider them bought with transformations, but the transformation is the body modification itself. For example, Bioluminescence works as a epidermal shift and Wings counts as Physiological Shift.<br /> <br /> What it means, well, it may cause some discomfort to people around you (it would anyway) what may cause increased difficulty on social interaction to people that don\u2019t like Novas or over reaction of Nova fans. It would cause anyway, so don\u2019t mater much anyway.<br /> <br /> Not all Body Modifications are visual, so things like Adhesive Grip may be left alone, as well as retractable claws and hidden gills. A more visible variation of those, like Adhesive grip make your fingers look like Geko ones, or claws that are always visible, would worth a minor transformation, while Gills that cover all your chest and are particularly sensitive to people putting hands inside my worth a physiological shift.<br /> <br /> Same can work for other Mega Edges, your body is covered in hard shell, it\u2019s Toughness with epidermic shift transformation, or even Hardened Skin mutation (why not both?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T03:05:19-08:00","id":1423706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1422990#post1422990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do have some concerns related to some rules (read Super Tech, and apply it all the way to Core),</div> </div> </div> </div>From someone just making their way through the books (including the core) right now, would you mind expanding on this somewhat?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11591-iron-seraph","name":"Iron Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T03:55:29-08:00","id":1423712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iron Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1423706#post1423706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From someone just making their way through the books (including the core) right now, would you mind expanding on this somewhat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea on what Supertech was build is great, the system to build it is interesting, with flaws happening spontaneously, instead of planned to make easier to build. I like it all! Even the fact you can buy a lot of items without needing the Artifact edge is a great way to make tech more available to players and justify why your car is different from everyone else.<br /> <br /> What I think is an issue is the way it was explained in general, you must read it many times to get the intention behind it, not because it is badly written, but because it should be more technical (less descriptive) to get the details correct, maybe step by step side bar and a better use of tables would solve it.<br /> <br /> It has a table of what a item of a certain rank can have (very useful!), and at same time it says it can\u2019t have all, with a comment that don\u2019t make much sense in the first reading: \u201cThe Storyguide may allow a combination of both, though the total number of dots shouldn\u2019t exceed the Enhancement rating for that Rank.\u201c It seams like the number of dots of edges, not the dots of equivalent item ranks, confusing at least, what they mean, as I understand is a rank 3 item can have enhancement 4, that can be exchanged by enhancement 3 and extras rank 1, or enhancement 1 and extras rank 3 (as enhancement 2 and extras equivalent to rank 2 would be a rank 2).<br /> <br /> The number of tags you can add to weapons, armors and vehicles is limited, below the number you get from regular items. The only advantage of an advance tech item is a lot of enhancements, what an armor don\u2019t use (unless you treat Enhancemnt as Soft Armor, what is not described anywhere), so a advanced car that is faster is hard to built, but a easy to maneuver is easy to built. If the idea is to build an specially tough armor as an Advanced tech item, you don\u2019t, the armor will cost more dots as a super tech item than dots in wealth to buy it.<br /> <br /> The same issue is carried along to Aberrant, but this time with an extra, Q-Tech x Nova Tech, and a huge text about transforming one in the other (that I like) that was left over when they decided you can build a Nova tech straight from your first plan (that I also like, what may sound contradictory). There is some stuff that is going to be reviewed in the Errata, so I will not talk much about it.<br /> <br /> Aexpansion have a better way to deal with it, with things being built as a sum of dots, with some negative characteristics counting as negative dots (different if flaws, that happen naturally). But it is designed to work only on the qualities related to psionics, not to add edges, not to add gifts, not to add enhancements when used as a tool, this kind of characteristics rely on the table described above. Scion (not in the main books, but in the companion) have a way to deal with it that is far better, similar to Aexpansion, but extending to all other characteristics, but it can\u2019t be used because Scion have no edges, gifts or doted ranks of powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-14-2020, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T08:23:19-08:00","id":1423742,"title":"","content":"Appreciated! <br /> <br /> I am torn on this book. It contains many ideas that I love (most of the updated setting, Collateral Damage etc) but has some problematic systems (the abovementioned Super-science, the near-nonsensical Scale chart for stuff like Mega-Brains). I feel like it needs a nontrivial patch of house rules/rewritten charts before it becomes playable.<br /> <br /> And that makes me sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11591-iron-seraph","name":"Iron Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T09:18:09-08:00","id":1423756,"title":"","content":"The problem of Scale is that it was intended to be open ended, and the examples don\u2019t help at all.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of the kinds of Scales are very interesting and gave a better understanding of their workings, but it\u2019s not clear on how exactly they interact.<br /> The best example is Leadership scale, I got it\u2019s about personal power, but one example of it in use would be absolutely useful. Not a example of what have this power, one example of it in use in game by a character, for example \u201cThe President of USA commanded people to do X, as he has Leadership scale 7 due to his position, he gains this and that in the roll, or affect this many people\u201d.<br /> The more practical examples of scale are Power and Durability, and even them are a bit hard to explain without example \u201cI am super strong, it don\u2019t mean I hit more often, just that I cause more damage when I hit\u201d. It\u2019s a bunch of small things that would be useful to have examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T11:58:15-08:00","id":1423798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1421233#post1421233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A comment on Scale on Attack and Defense:<br /> <br /> No power cause scale on attacks or defense, except Speed and only if the target is moving, not during a close combat fight. The scales apply only to damage, and durability don\u2019t make the targets more capable or dodging.<br /> <br /> Mega Might can cause much more damage, but the nova can\u2019t be particularly more capable in hitting just for being strong. The scale enhancements applies only to causing damage, including critical, what is particularly useful as you can also buy multiple injuries. So, don\u2019t hit often, but a hit can be lethal really fast...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure this is wrong, sorry. The example on Trinity Core page 111 has someone get a &quot;2 Enhancement bonus to his attacks, due to his superior Scale rating in power.&quot; All of the other descriptions seem to make it clear that it's a general Enhancement bonus, not an Enhancement bonus to the Inflict Damage stunt.<br /> <br /> If Power vs. Durability Scale only applied to damage, and you had to overcome a target's defense successes + 1 before you got that bonus, then abilities like Defense and Quantum Deflection would be a little more worthwhile. But if that's how they meant Scale to work, they forgot to write it anywhere, and the way they combine Defense and Soft Armor into one trait for antagonists mean it wouldn't work right anyway.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, a Mega-Might 3 nova will hit a Durability Scale 1 character almost all the time.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting that Stamina is used to avoid physical attacks, not Dexterity. So the initial attack roll isn't really a &quot;roll to hit&quot; so much as &quot;roll to overcome soak&quot; check anyway. You _can_ get Mega-Dexterity 5 and then spend another 60 XP to get Defense 5 so you get about +2 Enhancement to your defenses, but it's not really worthwhile when you could spend 60 XP to get Toughness 5 and get about +12 Enhancement to your defenses.<br /> <br /> Most of the game works well, but some things were either really poorly considered or really poorly explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","user":"Zeea","date":". 11-14-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T12:35:16-08:00","id":1423805,"title":"","content":"Ok, no problem, but Spider-man will suffer a lot when fighting Rhino, unless you give him Toughness (what don\u2019t sounds a Spider-Man thing) to represent his dodging capacity.<br /> <br /> Also, it will be really hard to hit a tank with a paintball, or even touch it during combat.<br /> <br /> My suggestion works fine to me. But yes, it\u2019s a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T12:48:02-08:00","id":1423810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1423805#post1423805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, no problem, but Spider-man will suffer a lot when fighting Rhino, unless you give him Toughness (what don\u2019t sounds a Spider-Man thing) to represent his dodging capacity.<br /> <br /> Also, it will be really hard to hit a tank with a paintball, or even touch it during combat.<br /> <br /> My suggestion works fine to me. But yes, it\u2019s a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I'm just talking about the official rules here. I'd argue that Spider-Man should have some Toughness, because he has Mega-Stamina and Mega-Might and has shrugged off some pretty solid hits, but he should be mostly Defense.<br /> <br /> I just did a house rule that makes Defense (the mega-edge) work just like Toughness and affect &quot;Durability&quot; Scale, except it doesn't work if you can't dodge, but also doesn't suffer certain drawbacks either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T16:12:16-08:00","id":1424108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1420548-aberrant-aberrant-in-november?p=1423712#post1423712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I think is an issue is the way it was explained in general, you must read it many times to get the intention behind it, not because it is badly written, but because it should be more technical (less descriptive) to get the details correct, maybe step by step side bar and a better use of tables would solve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't agree more. I don't think I've ever started a thread over here but was thinking that when the final, final Aberrant comes out I'd like to start a thread that encourages people to step-by-step particularly their Q-tech. Love that the Aberrant core book has the wink-wink Battingman &amp; Capital American &amp; Irony Mane &amp; Aunt-Mom gear. It feels like Mjolnir (esp the conduit to focusing Thur's powers version) would fit perfectly within the rules. However, I think I'd need a spectacular volume of hand-holding to get there. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}